a surprising character from 1883 has  returned to narrate the follow-up series  1923. here's why it's so meaningful for  Elsa Dunn to once again tell her  family's story spoilers for 1883 and the  first episode of 1923 ahead in the  Yellowstone prequel series 1883 James  Dunton and his wife Margaret ride from  Tennessee to Montana with their two  children Elsa and John nicknamed Jack  they make the difficult and arduous  Journey because they're seeking a better  life but by the time they arrive in  Montana many of their traveling parties  have died including Elsa while the  family is grieving the loss of their  daughter they decide to settle on the  land where she dies as it turns out the  tree under which she took her last  breath was also the place where John  Dutton warned the death of his oldest  son Lee in Yellowstone season one  viewers were devastated by Elsa's Ark  because so much of the series had  revolved around her many fans had been  convinced that after falling in love  with Ennis and losing her virginity to  him the family would discover she was  pregnant by the end of the season  unfortunately that wasn't the case  Ennis also died trying to protect them  Eric Nelson who played Ennis told TV  Insider we could have conquered the  world together but it wasn't in the  plans he also went on to praise the  realistic portrayal of the time period  adding we just see how quickly things  can change and so you can't take a  single second or day for granted also  narrated her family's perilous journey  to Montana in 1883 and she's doing the  same from beyond the grave in 1923.  foreshadowing what's to come for the  remaining duttons the 1883 season finale  ends with Elsa reuniting in death with  Sam the Comanche man she fell in love  with after Ennis died before the pair  raced through the planes Elsa's  voiceover explains there's a moment why  a dream sending memories March together  and form a perfect world that is heaven  Elsa may be gone but she isn't quite  done talking about her family or the  difficulties they face 1923 opens with  the same brutality that we've long come  to associate with the Yellowstone  Universe it doesn't waste time with  introductions instead immediately  jumping into the action we start with an  unknown man limping while he tries to  run obviously having been shot in the  leg we quickly realize that he's not  supposed to be on the Dutton land and  any sympathy we have for him dissipates  when we see that he's about to shoot our  protagonist Cara Dutton while she  screams in anguish after killing him  it's clear she's done this before Elsa's  voice over plainly states  violence has always haunted this family  reminding us that this sentiment is kind  of the dutton's motto Cara like the  duttons before and after isn't afraid to  do what's necessary for the ranch and  family from Elsa's voiceover we also  learned that her parents James and  Margaret had a second son Spencer before  meeting tragic fates of their own after  their deaths James brother Jacob and his  wife Cara took the boy in raised him and  built the Empire his brother dreamed of  viewers are given a major clue as to  what's to come in 1923 when Elsa States  my father had three children  [Music]  one would live to see their own children  grow while the season begins with both  brothers alive we now know one won't  survive the season but fans probably  shouldn't think that hint about the  events of 1923 has given anything away  Siri's Creator Taylor Sheridan is known  for taking story lines places no one  expects producer David glosser told The  Hollywood Reporter just before the 1883  finale aired it's never what you think  and the other shows we have coming up  this year there's never anything that's  on the nose Taylor believes in dropping  you right into a world and you're going  to be immersed in that world and  whatever you think is going to happen is  not going to happen  [Music]
 

